        ("How often should a lawn be mowed on Bribie Island?", "<p>Fortnightly from September to April and every four to six weeks in winter for most Bribie lawns. Reticulated lawns in Banksia Beach and the canal estates keep growing through winter and usually stay fortnightly. On sandy soil the interval depends more on water and feeding than on the calendar.</p>"),
        ("Do you look after holiday homes and rentals on Bribie?", "<p>Yes. Holiday houses in Woorim and Bongaree, villas and over-50s communities, and rentals managed from the mainland are a large part of our Bribie round. You do not need to be there; we mow on a set day, leave gates as we found them and message a photo when the job is done.</p>"),
        ("What is the best grass for Bribie Island?", "<p>Queensland blue couch for open, exposed blocks, and soft-leaf buffalo where there is some shelter from the sea breeze. Both need to be cut higher than inland and fed in spring and autumn, because the island's sand holds very little nutrient. Zoysia is a good low-maintenance option for small front lawns.</p>"),
